{:event/id "1105e98a-ad2e-422e-be8e-b1bd577b8bcb" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:2ab86fb4-5e36-403d-9358-8dafe4eb2b32" :event/seq 1 :event/causes ["2ab86fb4-5e36-403d-9358-8dafe4eb2b32"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:2ab86fb4-5e36-403d-9358-8dafe4eb2b32" :event/at "2026-09-06T13:52:49Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/passive-watch-coalesces-deltas-before-durable-work :finding/shapes #{:cell :queue :projection :reconciler} :finding/current-name "watcher-state + merge-watch-state/enqueue-watch-event! + maybe-queue-watched-jobs!" :finding/candidate-name "DebouncedDeltaAccumulator<Scope,Key>" :finding/claim "Knoxx keeps per-source passive-watch state in a process-local atom containing a snapshot, changed-path set, deleted-path set, and last-event timestamp. Both OS WatchService events and polling snapshot diffs feed this state. Repeated paths are coalesced by set membership and event order is not retained; changed and deleted classifications are accumulated independently, so the code does not prove mutual exclusion for one path. After a quiet debounce interval and only when no durable source job is already active, the accumulator materializes one ingestion job carrying sorted changed/deleted paths and clears the pending sets. This is a transient coordination accumulator that gates durable work, not an authoritative history or bounded queue."}}
{:event/id "559b3c96-88d2-4394-8d7e-cb293665a1f2" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:2ab86fb4-5e36-403d-9358-8dafe4eb2b32" :event/seq 2 :event/causes ["1105e98a-ad2e-422e-be8e-b1bd577b8bcb"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:2ab86fb4-5e36-403d-9358-8dafe4eb2b32" :event/at "2026-09-06T13:52:49Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/watch-registration-reconciles-desired-sources-with-live-handles :finding/shapes #{:registry :reconciler :driver :cell} :finding/current-name "sync-watch-registrations! + watch-keys + watched-sources" :finding/candidate-name "RegistrationReconciler<Desired,Handle>" :finding/claim "Knoxx derives a desired set of enabled local passive-watch sources from durable source configuration, compares it with process-local watched-source registrations, cancels and removes stale WatchKeys and their accumulator state, and registers missing source directory trees. The convergence target is set-like desired-versus-observed reconciliation, but observation, planning, OS-handle effects, and local registry mutation are interleaved in one function. It therefore pressure-tests ReconciliationPipeline: the domain law is reconciliation, while the current implementation does not satisfy the earlier pure-plan phase separation."}}
